176	///
177	/// Remove this possibility and make the signature unique.
178	///
179	/// Appendix F in the [Ethereum Yellow paper], defines the valid range for s in
180	/// (301): 0 < s < secp256k1n ÷ 2 + 1, and for v in (302): v ∈ {27, 28}.
181	///
182	/// Most signatures from current libraries generate a unique signature
183	/// with an s-value in the lower half order.
184	///
185	/// If your library generates malleable signatures,
186	/// such as s-values in the upper range, calculate a new s-value
187	/// with 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFEBAAEDCE6AF48A03BBFD25E8CD0364141 -
188	/// s1, and flip v from 27 to 28 or vice versa.
